    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0246" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1546a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-16T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6912. What action did Socialist Conference take respecting British participation
                    in Stockholm conference in case Germany is represented, also in case Germany not
                    represented? Department desires copy of secret proposal reported submitted by
                    Thomas to British Labor Party and Socialist Conference. Cable substance of this
                    proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
